<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Benadir</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Benadir coast</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Benadir is the southern coast of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalia">Somalia</a> on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a>, centred on the old trading towns of Mogadishu, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/marka">Merca</a> and Barawa. From medieval times these ports exported <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/ivory-trade">ivory</a>, hides and cloth across the Indian Ocean. In the 19th century the Sultanate of Zanzibar claimed them, and in 1892 it leased them to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italy">Italy</a>, forming the core of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/italian-somaliland">Italian Somaliland</a>; Banaadir is now a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somalis">Somali</a> region.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/benadir.jpg" alt="Benadir" width="320" height="240" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: VOA · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Mogadishu1d.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
